 "title": "Visiting Hours",
 "dates": "Wednesday, November 25 – Sunday, November 29, 2009",
 "logline": "Thanksgiving on Glenwood Avenue: a grandmother with one good hand, a guest asked to say grace, two hours without a phone in a room with vending machines — and a phone that won’t stop buzzing at the table.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "Nonna went up the stairs for her good rosary and came down the fast way. Your father drove her. Sober.",
   "if": "knows_nonna_fall"
  },
  {
   "text": "At the Starlite, a truck stop up the 101, she cast you as the Bible salesman and asked what believing is *like*.",
   "if": "skye_coffee"
  },
  {
   "text": "Against the Saab, slower than the first time. On purpose. She stopped it — her thumb on your mouth. “That’s for the plane.”",
   "if": "kissed_skye_2"
  },
  {
   "text": "Two holy cards for Nonna — Becca’s St. Raphael, Lena’s Our Lady of Prompt Succor. “Call me Thursday. After the pie. I want to hear Theo say *pop*.”",
   "if": "first_flight"
  },
  {
   "text": "At the gate, Becca: “I’m telling Mom at the table tomorrow. Then Facebook.”",
   "if": "becca_over"
  },
  {
   "text": "On the floor in Denver: “JACK. SHE’S ON TV.”",
   "if": "knows_skye_famous && gina_knows_skye"
  }
 ],
